// PolyBench/OpenMP heat-3d kernel, but improves spatial traversal:
//
//  - We work only on the interior i,j,k in [1, n-2] (as before).
//  - We apply 2D tiling in (i,j) on a large central rectangle using
//    noarr::into_blocks. This improves cache reuse in i/j while
//    preserving k as the innermost (contiguous) dimension.
//  - Edge strips and the corner that do not fit whole tiles are
//    handled separately via additional sliced traversals, so we do
//    not assume that (n-2) is divisible by the tile sizes.
